1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:02,079
(Penny:)Howard, I've asked you not to do that.

2
00:00:03,126 --> 00:00:05,626
Leslie and I do research together
at the university.

3
00:00:05,837 --> 00:00:08,007
(Penny:)Oh, wow. A girl scientist.

4
00:00:08,172 --> 00:00:10,462
(Lesley:)Yep. Come for the breasts,
stay for the brains.

5
00:00:11,384 --> 00:00:12,634
(Lesley:)So I'm glad I ran into you.

6
00:00:12,802 --> 00:00:15,512
(Lesley:)The Physics Department string quartet
needs a new cellist.

7
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:17,060
What happened to Elliott Wong?

8
00:00:17,223 --> 00:00:20,103
Switched over to high-energy
radiation research, had a mishap.

9
00:00:20,268 --> 00:00:23,188
(Lesley:)And now the other guys
are uncomfortable sitting next to him.

10
00:00:23,646 --> 00:00:25,566
(Lesley:)- So are you in?
- Yeah, sure. Why not?

11
00:00:25,731 --> 00:00:29,111
(Lesley:)- We rehearse on Tuesdays at your place.
- Why at my place?

12
00:00:29,277 --> 00:00:32,617
Yeah, Department of Energy said
our regular space is kind of a hot zone.

13
00:00:33,322 --> 00:00:35,412
(Lesley:)- Nice meeting you.
- Yeah, you too.

14
00:00:35,575 --> 00:00:37,785
(Penny:)Leonard, I didn't know
you played the cello.

15
00:00:37,952 --> 00:00:40,122
(Leonard:)Yeah, my parents felt
that naming me Leonard...

16
00:00:40,288 --> 00:00:42,578
(Leonard:)...and putting me
in advanced-placement classes...

17
00:00:42,748 --> 00:00:44,668
(Leonard:)...wasn't getting me beaten up enough.

18
00:00:45,418 --> 00:00:47,588
(Howard:)If you're into music, I happen
to be a human beatbox...

19
00:00:47,753 --> 00:00:49,333
(Howard:)- ...so...
- Really?

20
00:00:49,505 --> 00:00:51,505
[BEATBOXING]

21
00:00:56,179 --> 00:00:59,019
(Penny:)I'm actually not that into music.

